# Kumbi routing — F5 NGINX Ingress Controller (host-network ingress).
#
# The F5 NGINX Ingress Controller (namespace `nginx-ingress`) is the single
# front door for all environments. It runs with hostNetwork and binds the host
# ingress ports directly (no NodePort service, no k3s servicelb):
#
#   IngressClass `nginx`                  → controller nginx.org/ingress-controller
#   F5 NGINX IC Deployment                → binds host ports INGRESS_HTTP_PORT (HTTP) /
#                                            INGRESS_HTTPS_PORT (HTTPS) from kumbi-app-config
#                                            (e.g. dev HTTPS 11443, prod HTTPS 30003)
#   Ingress `kumbi-frontend`             → host ${DOMAIN} / → service frontend:80 (TLS kumbi-tls)
#   Ingress `kumbi-api`                  → host ${DOMAIN}/api + api.${DOMAIN} → service backend:8080
#
# TLS is terminated in the IC using the kumbi-tls secret (mkcert for dev/test,
# cert-manager for staging, supplied for prod).
#
# REACHABILITY (k3s node host IP, IC bound via hostNetwork):
#   https://kumbi.test/       → node :INGRESS_HTTPS_PORT → F5 NGINX IC → frontend
#   https://kumbi.test/api    → node :INGRESS_HTTPS_PORT → F5 NGINX IC → backend:8080
#   https://api.kumbi.test/   → node :INGRESS_HTTPS_PORT → F5 NGINX IC → backend:8080
#   (INGRESS_HTTPS_PORT is per-overlay: dev 11443, prod 30003; see kumbi-app-config)
#
# Optional host nginx: to publish on the standard 80/443 instead, run a host
# nginx that forwards 80→INGRESS_HTTP_PORT and 443→INGRESS_HTTPS_PORT (see
# infra/host/nginx-stream.conf, rendered by `make _ensure-hostroute`). Either way
# the service exposes itself on the host ingress ports — no need to discover
# ports after deploy; they are configured in kumbi-app-config (INGRESS_HTTP_PORT
# / INGRESS_HTTPS_PORT).
#
# Verify: `make ports ENV=dev` shows the ingress→service mapping and the host
# ports; `make k3s-check ENV=dev` confirms envoy/cilium/traefik are absent.
